1
00:00:12,659 --> 00:00:13,785
How have you been?

2
00:00:17,914 --> 00:00:19,082
Can we talk?

3
00:00:21,126 --> 00:00:21,960
Sure.

4
00:00:22,836 --> 00:00:23,837
We should.

5
00:00:26,881 --> 00:00:28,007
But before that…

6
00:00:28,091 --> 00:00:29,342
-Fucking…
-Wait!

7
00:00:30,009 --> 00:00:32,178
-Hear me out!
-You bastard!

8
00:00:39,018 --> 00:00:40,728
They're at it again. Fucking hell.

9
00:00:40,812 --> 00:00:43,982
What the fuck are the police doing,
letting people like that walk free?

10
00:00:44,065 --> 00:00:46,568
Hurry up and eat, you bitch!
Aren't you going to work?

11
00:00:47,068 --> 00:00:49,529
Always giving me shit. For fuck's sake.

12
00:01:00,373 --> 00:01:01,708
Come here, you bastard!

13
00:01:04,252 --> 00:01:05,378
Everyone out.

14
00:01:07,338 --> 00:01:09,424
Get the fuck out, you bastards!

15
00:01:11,217 --> 00:01:12,093
Wait.

16
00:01:13,094 --> 00:01:14,137
Don't go.

17
00:01:15,972 --> 00:01:18,850
It's gonna be a long night.

18
00:01:19,350 --> 00:01:21,561
Luckily, I have plenty of time tonight.

19
00:01:22,103 --> 00:01:23,188
You fucking piece of shit.

20
00:01:26,691 --> 00:01:27,525
Fuck!

21
00:01:36,034 --> 00:01:37,035
You're still alive?

22
00:01:37,118 --> 00:01:38,995
Thought you came here with a death wish.

23
00:01:39,078 --> 00:01:40,997
-Why aren't you dead yet?
-Your money.

24
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:43,499
You want it back, right?

25
00:01:46,544 --> 00:01:49,464
Is my money still alive?

26
00:01:49,964 --> 00:01:51,758
Find someone for me.

27
00:01:52,842 --> 00:01:54,802
Then I'll give you your money back.

28
00:02:04,687 --> 00:02:05,855
Look at this bastard.

29
00:02:05,939 --> 00:02:08,691
Fine. Who should I find?

30
00:02:11,069 --> 00:02:11,903
Me.

31
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:17,784
What the hell are you saying?

32
00:02:19,035 --> 00:02:20,078
Please

33
00:02:20,578 --> 00:02:21,746
find me.

34
00:02:23,957 --> 00:02:26,542
I lost myself.

35
00:02:29,379 --> 00:02:31,130
You fucking bastard.

36
00:02:35,176 --> 00:02:36,135
Please…

37
00:02:36,219 --> 00:02:39,013
Please find me.

38
00:03:15,925 --> 00:03:19,053
MOUSETRAP

39
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:21,681
I sent all the money we agreed on.

40
00:03:23,516 --> 00:03:25,143
We're done now, right?

41
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:26,978
Right, Moon-jae?

42
00:03:28,855 --> 00:03:29,856
Hello?

43
00:03:31,399 --> 00:03:32,358
Hello?

44
00:03:34,277 --> 00:03:36,988
Stay sharp until it's all wrapped up.

45
00:03:37,488 --> 00:03:39,574
Just hang in there until then.

46
00:03:40,074 --> 00:03:42,076
Okay. Don't worry.

47
00:03:43,244 --> 00:03:45,246
Oh, but we…

48
00:03:57,383 --> 00:03:58,384
So,

49
00:03:59,344 --> 00:04:02,013
you got cleaned out
by a guy who looks exactly like you?

50
00:04:02,096 --> 00:04:04,057
Your house, money, everything?

51
00:04:06,392 --> 00:04:07,769
You expect me to believe that?

52
00:04:08,269 --> 00:04:11,147
You bastard, if you were me,
would you just believe that?

53
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:12,857
I can't believe it either.

54
00:04:14,484 --> 00:04:15,985
But it's true.

55
00:04:17,278 --> 00:04:19,614
There's nothing left in my name.

56
00:04:20,114 --> 00:04:21,908
That bastard even changed my ID number.

57
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:25,244
Officially, I'm not Je Moon-jae anymore.

58
00:04:26,037 --> 00:04:27,830
I'm just an empty shell.

59
00:04:29,540 --> 00:04:32,752
A person who doesn't exist, dead or alive.

60
00:04:36,047 --> 00:04:37,131
I have to catch him.

61
00:04:39,342 --> 00:04:40,760
The bastard who looks like me.

62
00:04:40,843 --> 00:04:45,181
You're the only one
who can prove I'm Je Moon-jae.

63
00:04:47,392 --> 00:04:48,893
And only you can help me.

64
00:04:49,394 --> 00:04:52,313
Why the fuck would I help you?
I should be killing you, you asshole.

65
00:04:52,397 --> 00:04:55,191
You need to find your money.
And I need to find my name.

66
00:04:58,069 --> 00:04:59,821
I have more than enough money.

67
00:04:59,904 --> 00:05:01,489
Money isn't the issue for me.

68
00:05:01,572 --> 00:05:03,825
Okay? Life is.

69
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:06,869
I've gotten tired of it, you see.

70
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:09,247
All you need to do is write.

71
00:05:09,330 --> 00:05:10,289
Give me the rights,

72
00:05:10,373 --> 00:05:13,751
and I'll make it take off, film or TV.

73
00:05:13,835 --> 00:05:15,378
-Okay?
-Okay.

74
00:05:20,174 --> 00:05:21,134
If I'm lying, Noja,

75
00:05:21,801 --> 00:05:22,718
beat me to death.

76
00:05:22,802 --> 00:05:24,387
Why do you keep calling me Noja?

77
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:27,056
Am I your friend or something,
you bastard?

78
00:05:28,558 --> 00:05:30,143
You told me to use your name.

79
00:05:33,354 --> 00:05:34,522
Is this your place?

80
00:05:37,692 --> 00:05:38,526
Here.

81
00:05:39,444 --> 00:05:40,278
What's this?

82
00:05:40,361 --> 00:05:42,905
I got one for you.
Go write something good.

83
00:05:42,989 --> 00:05:44,365
I already have a laptop.

84
00:05:44,449 --> 00:05:47,869
Just use this one.
We're in the same boat now.

85
00:05:50,163 --> 00:05:51,247
Thank you, sir.

86
00:05:51,330 --> 00:05:52,623
For God's sake.

87
00:05:52,707 --> 00:05:54,375
"Sir"? Are we thugs or what?

88
00:05:54,459 --> 00:05:56,085
Just call me Noja.

89
00:05:57,086 --> 00:05:58,087
Okay, Noja.

90
00:05:59,505 --> 00:06:02,925
Finding people?
Don't worry. I'm an expert.

91
00:06:04,385 --> 00:06:07,388
But if you screw me over again,

92
00:06:09,015 --> 00:06:10,558
you'll suffer a long, slow death.

93
00:06:10,641 --> 00:06:12,185
You won't die easily.

94
00:06:13,478 --> 00:06:16,772
I spent three fucking years
looking for this bastard.

95
00:06:16,856 --> 00:06:19,442
Now I have to find another one
who looks exactly like him?

96
00:06:19,525 --> 00:06:22,236
You gotta be fucking kidding me.

97
00:06:22,904 --> 00:06:24,363
We must find someone else first.

98
00:06:25,948 --> 00:06:28,242
Fucking hell.

99
00:06:28,326 --> 00:06:29,702
Who is it now?

100
00:06:29,785 --> 00:06:32,497
My friend who had me skim money off you.

101
00:06:32,580 --> 00:06:34,415
It'll be faster to find him first.

102
00:06:34,916 --> 00:06:36,000
They're in it together.

103
00:06:36,083 --> 00:06:37,752
Jesus, how…

104
00:06:38,544 --> 00:06:41,339
How the fuck did I get mixed up
with this bastard?

105
00:06:48,513 --> 00:06:49,347
Listen carefully.

106
00:06:50,223 --> 00:06:52,433
You're my hostage now.

107
00:06:53,351 --> 00:06:56,938
If I find my money, you live.
If I don't, you fucking die. Got it?

108
00:06:57,647 --> 00:07:00,274
Do everything you can to help me
if you want to live.

109
00:07:03,903 --> 00:07:05,446
-Okay.
-Damn it!

110
00:07:06,781 --> 00:07:08,074
Goddamn it.

111
00:07:30,179 --> 00:07:32,098
Do you really have to go this far?

112
00:07:32,181 --> 00:07:34,392
How am I supposed to sleep like this?

113
00:07:38,938 --> 00:07:40,773
Can't you at least loosen it a bit?

114
00:08:07,174 --> 00:08:09,010
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

115
00:08:10,595 --> 00:08:11,470
What?

116
00:08:12,138 --> 00:08:13,389
He got caught already?

117
00:08:18,686 --> 00:08:19,520
Huh?

118
00:08:25,109 --> 00:08:27,612
Oh, he went there on his own.

119
00:08:31,532 --> 00:08:32,992
This is getting interesting.

120
00:08:43,294 --> 00:08:45,254
Excuse me?

121
00:08:48,591 --> 00:08:51,177
We're not open yet. Lunch starts at noon.

122
00:08:51,260 --> 00:08:53,554
Oh, I'm not here to eat.

123
00:08:54,263 --> 00:08:55,931
You know Mr. Kim Yeong-geun, right?

124
00:08:56,432 --> 00:08:59,018
Could you tell me where he is?

125
00:09:01,771 --> 00:09:02,855
Sir?

126
00:09:06,108 --> 00:09:07,818
Who even is that?

127
00:09:08,486 --> 00:09:09,320
Huh?

128
00:09:10,196 --> 00:09:11,822
I heard you used to work together.

129
00:09:13,032 --> 00:09:14,283
Oh, come on.

130
00:09:14,784 --> 00:09:17,328
Don't be like that.
If you know, just tell me.

131
00:09:17,411 --> 00:09:19,121
Where are you from?

132
00:09:19,205 --> 00:09:21,040
I'm with the police.

133
00:09:27,213 --> 00:09:31,008
Jeez, don't bother the guy.
He's clean now.

134
00:09:31,092 --> 00:09:32,343
God.

135
00:09:32,426 --> 00:09:34,679
What, you think other people
don't live clean?

136
00:09:35,471 --> 00:09:38,891
Just tell me where your "clean" guy is.

137
00:09:41,018 --> 00:09:43,854
It's nothing serious.
It'll just take a minute.

138
00:09:43,938 --> 00:09:45,606
I just need to see him for a moment.

139
00:09:48,150 --> 00:09:49,443
What's this about?

140
00:09:50,152 --> 00:09:52,780
I came because he didn't pay a fine.

141
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:54,240
A fine?

142
00:09:54,323 --> 00:09:56,992
A summary summons. Why won't he take it?

143
00:09:57,076 --> 00:09:58,828
The fine's not even 200,000 won.

144
00:09:58,911 --> 00:10:02,415
If he keeps this up, his assets
could get seized over a 200,000-won fine.

145
00:10:02,915 --> 00:10:04,291
I'm busy as hell already.

146
00:10:08,629 --> 00:10:09,964
Have a good one!

147
00:10:16,721 --> 00:10:19,598
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

148
00:10:27,857 --> 00:10:31,444
I'd be retired by now
if I'd put that money into real estate.

149
00:10:33,904 --> 00:10:36,240
That no-good bastard.

150
00:10:36,824 --> 00:10:39,326
How did I end up
getting mixed up with him?

151
00:10:41,328 --> 00:10:44,373
To become a new man…
I was crazy to trust him.

152
00:10:44,457 --> 00:10:46,751
If a thug becomes a businessman,

153
00:10:47,251 --> 00:10:49,086
does that make him a new man?

154
00:10:50,171 --> 00:10:51,881
That's basically identity fraud.

155
00:10:53,174 --> 00:10:55,718
Don't push it.

156
00:10:55,801 --> 00:10:56,635
Okay?

157
00:10:56,719 --> 00:11:00,514
Because of you, I never became a new man.
I'm still the same old me, you bastard.

158
00:11:00,598 --> 00:11:02,767
I'm a dangerous man. You hear me?

159
00:11:03,476 --> 00:11:05,227
What is he blabbering about?

160
00:11:06,687 --> 00:11:08,147
All right. Let's go.

161
00:11:09,398 --> 00:11:12,443
To catch the bastard who stole
from the bastard who stole from me.

162
00:11:24,747 --> 00:11:29,084
His address might be registered with
the accountants' association or something.

163
00:11:29,668 --> 00:11:32,379
For lawyers and accountants,
associations are important.

164
00:11:37,009 --> 00:11:38,010
Are you listening?

165
00:11:39,011 --> 00:11:40,304
Yeah. I hear you!

166
00:11:40,888 --> 00:11:43,808
But I've got a plan too, so just zip it.

167
00:11:45,309 --> 00:11:46,435
Where are we going?

168
00:11:48,521 --> 00:11:50,856
We're on our way
to meet the blog owner you found.

169
00:11:51,524 --> 00:11:55,402
The one who posted the reunion photos.
That's how you got to the reunion, right?

170
00:11:55,986 --> 00:11:57,071
You know where he is?

171
00:11:57,154 --> 00:12:02,076
Know what's wrong with kids these days?
They put their personal info everywhere.

172
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:05,496
Blog, Instagram.
His personal info is everywhere.

173
00:12:05,579 --> 00:12:07,498
These days, if you hack someone's phone,

174
00:12:07,581 --> 00:12:10,668
you can clean them out in an instant.

175
00:12:11,377 --> 00:12:13,504
Don't ever post stuff online.

176
00:12:15,673 --> 00:12:18,634
Criminals and would-be criminals
shouldn't do that.

177
00:12:18,717 --> 00:12:19,635
Got it?

178
00:12:22,179 --> 00:12:23,556
BOARD-CERTIFIED PLASTIC SURGEON, MD

179
00:12:24,390 --> 00:12:27,017
Wow, you must be pretty good with a knife.

180
00:12:27,101 --> 00:12:30,396
You're basically creating faces
from scratch, huh?

181
00:12:30,479 --> 00:12:32,523
This is straight-up identity fraud.

182
00:12:32,606 --> 00:12:36,986
Isn't that illegal,
changing someone's face like that?

183
00:12:37,069 --> 00:12:38,153
-Damn it.
-Huh?

184
00:12:38,237 --> 00:12:40,239
Kyeong-tae. You really don't remember me?

185
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:43,117
It's me, Moon-jae. Je Moon-jae.
And you're…

186
00:12:44,034 --> 00:12:46,078
You're Jeon Kyeong-tae.
Your last name, Jeon.

187
00:12:46,161 --> 00:12:47,580
You really don't remember me?

188
00:12:47,663 --> 00:12:49,999
What do you two think you're doing?
Seriously?

189
00:12:50,583 --> 00:12:52,042
Then call the police.

190
00:12:52,543 --> 00:12:55,462
What, you think I won't call the police?

191
00:12:57,464 --> 00:12:58,591
What are you trying to--

192
00:13:00,467 --> 00:13:02,469
How about some plastic surgery, Doc?

193
00:13:08,601 --> 00:13:09,768
SON SOO-HYUN

194
00:13:11,395 --> 00:13:15,316
The number you've dialed does not exist.
Please check and try again.

195
00:13:15,399 --> 00:13:17,651
That bastard totally went off the grid.

196
00:13:18,569 --> 00:13:20,112
This guy's not involved.

197
00:13:25,242 --> 00:13:26,702
You can't go to crowded places.

198
00:13:26,785 --> 00:13:29,872
You can't go to open spaces,
and you don't like tight spaces either.

199
00:13:29,955 --> 00:13:33,042
You've got so many fucking issues.

200
00:13:33,125 --> 00:13:35,252
Burgers taste best at the joint.

201
00:13:37,755 --> 00:13:40,549
Sometimes you're fine,
sometimes you're not.

202
00:13:42,051 --> 00:13:44,553
It's all because of your guilt, punk.

203
00:13:44,637 --> 00:13:46,430
The guilt of running off with my money!

204
00:13:54,897 --> 00:13:56,899
I need my meds.

205
00:13:58,067 --> 00:14:01,612
I'm anxious. I never know
when the symptoms will flare up.

206
00:14:01,695 --> 00:14:03,572
You said you need a prescription.

207
00:14:03,656 --> 00:14:06,951
Why didn't you get that doctor
to write you one, you dumbass?

208
00:14:10,829 --> 00:14:13,290
Soo-hyun always got them for me. Damn it.

209
00:14:24,802 --> 00:14:27,388
Why are you looking at me?
Am I your errand boy, punk?

210
00:14:28,347 --> 00:14:29,515
Did somebody say that?

211
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:32,267
Aren't we on the same team?

212
00:14:32,351 --> 00:14:34,228
We're in the same boat!

213
00:14:34,311 --> 00:14:37,022
You no-good bastard. Seriously.

214
00:14:42,361 --> 00:14:43,362
Move aside.

215
00:14:45,781 --> 00:14:47,992
Just take these and get by for now.

216
00:14:49,994 --> 00:14:50,828
What's this?

217
00:14:51,412 --> 00:14:54,289
One's a painkiller.
I don't know what the other one is.

218
00:14:56,583 --> 00:15:00,045
I can't just take any meds.

219
00:15:00,963 --> 00:15:03,590
You don't know the story
of Wonhyo and the skull water?

220
00:15:03,674 --> 00:15:05,592
It's all about how you take it, punk!

221
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:14,101
Who's that bastard impersonating me?

222
00:15:17,438 --> 00:15:20,774
Soo-hyun brought him to the reunion
about a year ago.

223
00:15:20,858 --> 00:15:22,735
At first, we didn't recognize him,

224
00:15:22,818 --> 00:15:25,279
but then he looked like the guy
in the graduation pic.

225
00:15:25,863 --> 00:15:27,406
So we thought he was Moon-jae.

226
00:15:28,407 --> 00:15:30,534
See? They're in this together.

227
00:15:30,617 --> 00:15:32,745
But this doesn't make any sense.

228
00:15:33,245 --> 00:15:35,831
I've had drinks with Moon-jae
so many times recently.

229
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:39,001
Turns out, he's a famous writer.

230
00:15:41,587 --> 00:15:42,713
But

231
00:15:43,338 --> 00:15:46,508
you don't even remember
what happened on our school trip.

232
00:15:47,009 --> 00:15:48,969
That's not something you forget!

233
00:15:49,470 --> 00:15:51,096
Moon-jae remembered it clearly.

234
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,892
You keep going on about some school trip.
What about it?

235
00:15:54,975 --> 00:15:57,561
What happened? Let's hear it. What is it?

236
00:15:58,896 --> 00:16:00,898
There was a fire.

237
00:16:02,232 --> 00:16:05,402
All the students had to evacuate.
It was a total mess.

238
00:16:08,655 --> 00:16:10,282
And you don't remember that?

239
00:16:12,034 --> 00:16:13,368
Does that make sense?

240
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:29,968
You are Je Moon-jae, right?

241
00:16:34,932 --> 00:16:37,226
And he got plastic surgery
just for the money?

242
00:16:38,435 --> 00:16:40,354
Why? He could've just taken it all.

243
00:16:40,437 --> 00:16:42,940
You said it was in that bastard's account.

244
00:16:44,691 --> 00:16:47,694
Because it was Je Moon-jae's money.

245
00:16:48,403 --> 00:16:51,031
And I'm not Je Moon-jae anymore.

246
00:16:53,242 --> 00:16:56,203
Even if you go to the police,
you'd be a Je Moon-jae impersonator?

247
00:16:56,286 --> 00:16:57,496
I guess so.

248
00:16:58,413 --> 00:17:03,168
And he lured me with a card in your name
so I could find you, huh?

249
00:17:03,252 --> 00:17:05,712
Because I'd kill you if I caught you.

250
00:17:05,796 --> 00:17:07,381
I'd be doing his dirty work.

251
00:17:08,215 --> 00:17:10,092
Then why did he warn me to run?

252
00:17:10,175 --> 00:17:12,302
Why not just let you kill me?

253
00:17:12,803 --> 00:17:14,680
Maybe the job's not done yet.

254
00:17:14,763 --> 00:17:17,683
Maybe he hasn't moved all the money.

255
00:17:21,186 --> 00:17:22,271
That could be it.

256
00:17:26,900 --> 00:17:28,694
That's an interesting bastard.

257
00:17:33,115 --> 00:17:34,783
You mean "bastards."

258
00:17:36,034 --> 00:17:38,162
You little shit.

259
00:17:38,245 --> 00:17:39,329
Where are we going now?

260
00:17:46,587 --> 00:17:48,005
Hey, where are we going?

261
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:03,270
I told you. This is a waste of time.
I've been here before.

262
00:18:03,353 --> 00:18:05,814
You only see what you know.

263
00:18:07,941 --> 00:18:08,775
I mean…

264
00:18:11,695 --> 00:18:13,030
You coming?

265
00:18:31,757 --> 00:18:32,591
It's just…

266
00:18:34,426 --> 00:18:35,636
Elevators are a bit…

267
00:18:36,678 --> 00:18:38,347
What a load of bullshit.

268
00:18:41,433 --> 00:18:43,185
Must be great exercise.

269
00:18:56,114 --> 00:18:57,824
If you scratch someone's car,

270
00:18:57,908 --> 00:19:00,452
any civilized person
would leave their number.

271
00:19:00,535 --> 00:19:03,830
You accountants are all educated, right?
Am I wrong?

272
00:19:04,331 --> 00:19:05,958
What's this country coming to?

273
00:19:06,041 --> 00:19:06,917
Just a moment.

274
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,920
He doesn't work here anymore.
I'll check the parking log to…

275
00:19:10,003 --> 00:19:13,423
Here it is. A white BMW. Is that correct?

276
00:19:13,507 --> 00:19:15,008
-Yes, white.
-Okay.

277
00:19:15,092 --> 00:19:18,262
-What's that bastard's plate number?
-The plate number is…

278
00:19:20,681 --> 00:19:23,308
Hey, we're done here. See you downstairs.

279
00:19:37,239 --> 00:19:39,157
No, that's not it.

280
00:19:41,159 --> 00:19:43,453
Yeah, white. 5340.

281
00:19:43,537 --> 00:19:45,580
Got it. Find out fast!

282
00:19:50,711 --> 00:19:51,837
Did you find him?

283
00:19:55,674 --> 00:19:59,011
ENTER AMOUNT
2,000,000 WON

284
00:19:59,094 --> 00:19:59,970
Okay.

285
00:20:00,679 --> 00:20:02,097
I asked if you found it.

286
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:04,891
Fuck, you've gotta wait.

287
00:20:04,975 --> 00:20:06,018
For who?

288
00:20:06,101 --> 00:20:08,353
None of your business.
It's a trade secret.

289
00:20:23,243 --> 00:20:24,536
WHITE BMW 5340
1,500,000 WON REWARD

290
00:20:29,291 --> 00:20:30,167
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

291
00:20:51,521 --> 00:20:52,522
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

292
00:21:32,062 --> 00:21:33,730
Money exchange, huh?

293
00:21:36,024 --> 00:21:37,567
Shit, I screwed up.

294
00:21:38,485 --> 00:21:40,946
I guess you can smoke in here.

295
00:21:42,197 --> 00:21:43,323
Oh, that's great.

296
00:21:47,452 --> 00:21:48,995
Oh, you can't?

297
00:21:53,291 --> 00:21:54,626
What is this place?

298
00:21:55,710 --> 00:21:57,712
What do you mean? It's just an office.

299
00:21:57,796 --> 00:21:58,922
Why?

300
00:21:59,005 --> 00:21:59,923
Oh, come on.

301
00:22:00,006 --> 00:22:03,051
What kind of office has no computers?

302
00:22:03,635 --> 00:22:04,511
Hi.

303
00:22:05,095 --> 00:22:06,346
-Hey, babe.
-Yeah.

304
00:22:06,430 --> 00:22:07,514
Hello.

305
00:22:07,597 --> 00:22:08,473
Look.

306
00:22:08,557 --> 00:22:11,351
I'm not interested
in your illegal escort stuff, okay?

307
00:22:11,435 --> 00:22:13,520
Are you close with the guys upstairs?

308
00:22:14,813 --> 00:22:16,857
-Why?
-I'm just interested.

309
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,567
I don't wanna get involved.

310
00:22:18,650 --> 00:22:19,901
And you won't be.

311
00:22:19,985 --> 00:22:22,571
Don't worry.
My life is already complicated enough.

312
00:22:24,573 --> 00:22:26,533
I'm not lying.

313
00:22:28,285 --> 00:22:30,120
I hear he finds people for a living.

314
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:32,456
Well, it's a private detective agency.

315
00:22:33,081 --> 00:22:33,915
He's different.

316
00:22:34,416 --> 00:22:36,209
He can even find unidentified people.

317
00:22:36,293 --> 00:22:40,088
Even if you hide from your debts,
he'll track you down in no time.

318
00:22:40,172 --> 00:22:43,216
You know those guys
who run online gambling sites?

319
00:22:43,300 --> 00:22:45,469
-Yeah.
-They come around a lot.

320
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:48,972
They really went after someone yesterday.

321
00:22:49,055 --> 00:22:52,100
But if they beat up people like that,

322
00:22:52,184 --> 00:22:53,393
wouldn't they die?

323
00:22:54,686 --> 00:22:56,188
They probably would.

324
00:22:58,148 --> 00:22:59,483
Anyway,

325
00:22:59,983 --> 00:23:02,152
don't let him know I said this.

326
00:23:02,819 --> 00:23:04,696
He looks scary as hell.

327
00:23:04,779 --> 00:23:07,699
I get scared
every time I see him in the hallway.

328
00:23:09,451 --> 00:23:12,245
It must've been hard for you. Here.

329
00:23:12,871 --> 00:23:14,456
PARK SUN-YONG

330
00:23:15,415 --> 00:23:17,209
Let's keep in touch, okay?

331
00:23:18,710 --> 00:23:21,505
Fuck. You said I wouldn't be involved.

332
00:23:21,588 --> 00:23:23,381
I'm just interested.

333
00:23:25,634 --> 00:23:26,468
Take care.

334
00:23:29,179 --> 00:23:30,263
The fuck?

335
00:23:45,362 --> 00:23:50,575
EVERYTHING WILL BE FINE, SO DON'T WORRY
IT'S ALMOST OVER, OKAY?

336
00:23:57,582 --> 00:23:59,042
It's almost over.

337
00:23:59,709 --> 00:24:01,628
It's almost over.

338
00:24:12,889 --> 00:24:14,099
5340?

339
00:24:15,976 --> 00:24:19,020
SEOUL DELIVERY RIDERS ASSOCIATION
WHITE BMW 5340 WANTED

340
00:24:32,659 --> 00:24:35,662
The Heart Sutra
has nothing to do with Noja.

341
00:24:36,913 --> 00:24:39,624
Just listen and be grateful, damn it.

342
00:24:40,292 --> 00:24:42,002
It's why you're still alive.

343
00:24:44,546 --> 00:24:46,881
But why does this bastard look familiar?

344
00:24:47,382 --> 00:24:49,509
Maybe it's because he looks so plain?

345
00:24:49,593 --> 00:24:52,971
I'm surprised
he's still active on social media.

346
00:24:53,054 --> 00:24:54,723
It's private now.

347
00:24:54,806 --> 00:24:58,059
I downloaded this early this morning.

348
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:00,645
Early this morning?

349
00:25:01,771 --> 00:25:02,689
You're diligent.

350
00:25:02,772 --> 00:25:05,692
You gotta be more diligent
than the ones who ran off.

351
00:25:05,775 --> 00:25:08,987
Nothing in life is easy. Okay?

352
00:25:10,322 --> 00:25:13,450
Everything's tough and exhausting.
That's life.

353
00:25:14,409 --> 00:25:16,161
So you were lazy chasing me, huh?

354
00:25:17,037 --> 00:25:19,122
You hid out for three years.

355
00:25:19,205 --> 00:25:21,833
How was I supposed to catch you,
you little shit?

356
00:25:22,334 --> 00:25:23,335
Damn it.

357
00:25:27,547 --> 00:25:28,381
Hello?

358
00:25:30,091 --> 00:25:31,176
Yeah. Okay.

359
00:25:31,676 --> 00:25:33,345
Send me the address.

360
00:25:35,347 --> 00:25:37,265
What? They already found him?

361
00:25:39,601 --> 00:25:40,935
But he's still in Seoul.

362
00:25:41,519 --> 00:25:42,979
Why didn't he run?

363
00:25:43,563 --> 00:25:45,440
If I were him, I'd have run by now.

364
00:25:45,523 --> 00:25:47,609
You were right. He's still got loose ends.

365
00:26:18,556 --> 00:26:19,557
Who are you?

366
00:26:20,183 --> 00:26:21,434
You know me?

367
00:26:24,270 --> 00:26:25,146
What is it?

368
00:26:36,783 --> 00:26:39,994
RUN AWAY. RIGHT NOW.

369
00:27:15,363 --> 00:27:16,489
Goddamn it.

370
00:27:17,157 --> 00:27:18,283
Just stay here, punk!

371
00:27:19,784 --> 00:27:21,077
Shit.

372
00:27:33,465 --> 00:27:34,466
Damn it.

373
00:27:51,191 --> 00:27:52,776
Fuck!

374
00:28:03,453 --> 00:28:04,454
Damn it.

375
00:28:11,377 --> 00:28:12,796
Hey, punk. You good?

376
00:28:15,340 --> 00:28:17,091
God, you no-good bastard. Seriously.

377
00:28:22,347 --> 00:28:24,641
You said that bastard
had a guy tailing me, right?

378
00:28:24,724 --> 00:28:25,683
Yeah.

379
00:28:25,767 --> 00:28:28,228
He was tailing me a couple of days ago.
I ran into him.

380
00:28:28,311 --> 00:28:30,355
I should've roughed that bastard up more.

381
00:28:30,438 --> 00:28:33,274
How was I supposed to know
that bastard was him?

382
00:28:33,358 --> 00:28:34,984
He even ditched his car.

383
00:28:35,485 --> 00:28:36,986
He must've been in a hurry.

384
00:28:37,070 --> 00:28:38,530
So we wait here for him?

385
00:28:40,907 --> 00:28:42,283
What if he doesn't come back?

386
00:28:51,543 --> 00:28:53,294
But it's strange.

387
00:28:53,795 --> 00:28:55,505
The timing is just too perfect.

388
00:28:55,588 --> 00:29:01,135
Huh? How did he stay one step ahead of us?

389
00:29:17,235 --> 00:29:18,611
There's not much there.

390
00:29:19,487 --> 00:29:21,364
There's a lot here!

391
00:29:22,156 --> 00:29:23,616
Look at the dates, you punk!

392
00:29:23,700 --> 00:29:25,451
These are all from a few days ago!

393
00:29:25,535 --> 00:29:27,704
He's had his dashcam off for days.

394
00:29:27,787 --> 00:29:31,374
He knew someone would search the car
if things went south.

395
00:29:37,213 --> 00:29:38,923
What do we do now?

396
00:29:39,966 --> 00:29:41,342
You've got a plan B, right?

397
00:29:41,426 --> 00:29:43,553
You said you're an expert
at finding people.

398
00:29:47,432 --> 00:29:49,225
-That'll be 70,000 won.
-Right.

399
00:29:52,145 --> 00:29:53,479
That'll be 2,000,000 today.

400
00:29:53,563 --> 00:29:56,441
Gas, food, my time, and all that.

401
00:29:56,524 --> 00:29:58,985
You'll be charged for all this.
You know that, right?

402
00:29:59,068 --> 00:30:02,780
If a client hires a private detective,
they should pay up.

403
00:30:07,702 --> 00:30:09,495
Client? You said I'm your hostage.

404
00:30:09,996 --> 00:30:11,080
You're both.

405
00:30:14,751 --> 00:30:15,585
Where to?

406
00:30:15,668 --> 00:30:17,253
What's it to you?

407
00:30:17,337 --> 00:30:21,507
I don't care if I'm a hostage or a client.
Just tell me where we're going!

408
00:30:23,843 --> 00:30:26,429
We're going with plan B, you punk.
Happy now?

409
00:30:39,275 --> 00:30:44,113
Those who run can hide themselves,
but they can't hide their families.

410
00:30:44,197 --> 00:30:45,198
Why?

411
00:30:45,281 --> 00:30:48,117
Even within a family,
each person has their own life.

412
00:30:49,911 --> 00:30:52,246
How did you know Soo-hyun's kid goes here?

413
00:30:52,330 --> 00:30:53,623
Instagram.

414
00:30:54,207 --> 00:30:55,959
That damn Instagram.

415
00:30:57,168 --> 00:30:59,295
-Where to?
-Aren't we here for his address?

416
00:30:59,379 --> 00:31:02,131
You think they'll just tell you?
They don't know you.

417
00:31:02,215 --> 00:31:04,884
You really don't know
how the world works, do you?

418
00:31:04,968 --> 00:31:05,802
Close the door!

419
00:31:06,844 --> 00:31:07,679
Open that.

420
00:31:09,514 --> 00:31:10,974
Give me one. Hurry.

421
00:31:17,230 --> 00:31:19,732
What's all this?

422
00:31:19,816 --> 00:31:21,109
This one's way too far.

423
00:31:21,192 --> 00:31:23,778
Give me a closer one. One in Seoul.

424
00:31:23,861 --> 00:31:25,655
Seoul. Right.

425
00:31:27,949 --> 00:31:29,158
SEOUL MAPO POLICE STATION

426
00:31:30,868 --> 00:31:32,036
Stay here.

427
00:31:33,037 --> 00:31:33,997
Why?

428
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:36,791
Just stay here, punk!
Ever seen a detective in sweats?

429
00:31:44,590 --> 00:31:48,219
Da-eun hasn't been in for a few days.

430
00:31:48,302 --> 00:31:51,681
So I called her mother,
and she said Da-eun's taking a break.

431
00:31:51,764 --> 00:31:53,641
Seems like it's a family matter.

432
00:31:54,475 --> 00:31:56,185
What kind of family matter?

433
00:31:56,269 --> 00:31:57,186
I'm not sure.

434
00:31:57,270 --> 00:32:00,023
She just said
Da-eun's taking a break for a while.

435
00:32:02,316 --> 00:32:05,278
I guess I'll have to go to this address
and ask myself.

436
00:32:05,862 --> 00:32:07,780
What's this about?

437
00:32:07,864 --> 00:32:10,616
Da-eun's parents aren't the kind
to commit a crime.

438
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:15,121
It's always the ones you least suspect
who do it.

439
00:32:15,621 --> 00:32:17,540
All right. Thank you for your cooperation.

440
00:32:19,333 --> 00:32:20,418
Crap.

441
00:32:25,089 --> 00:32:26,340
We're with the police.

442
00:32:27,091 --> 00:32:29,635
Well. We're with the police.

443
00:32:31,220 --> 00:32:32,221
What's wrong with him?

444
00:32:34,265 --> 00:32:35,725
-What's going on?
-What?

445
00:32:35,808 --> 00:32:37,101
Why are the police here?

446
00:32:37,185 --> 00:32:38,561
What? Hey!

447
00:32:38,644 --> 00:32:39,687
Slow down!

448
00:32:41,064 --> 00:32:42,774
What's wrong? Someone's there!

449
00:32:43,649 --> 00:32:45,777
What the hell is going on here?

450
00:32:51,491 --> 00:32:53,868
-Hey, did you see something?
-No.

451
00:32:53,951 --> 00:32:55,536
Jeez.

452
00:32:55,620 --> 00:32:56,954
Move, damn it.

453
00:32:58,372 --> 00:32:59,582
Goddamn it.

454
00:33:02,543 --> 00:33:03,461
It's so quiet.

455
00:33:04,087 --> 00:33:06,631
The cops even went to the daycare.
No way they are home.

456
00:33:09,967 --> 00:33:11,135
Cops! Get down!

457
00:33:11,636 --> 00:33:14,305
-Cops! Get the hell down.
-Cops?

458
00:33:16,808 --> 00:33:17,683
They're gone.

459
00:33:19,185 --> 00:33:22,605
I didn't even report him.
Why did the police come for Soo-hyun?

460
00:33:23,439 --> 00:33:24,273
Yeah.

461
00:33:24,857 --> 00:33:26,400
What the hell has he been up to?

462
00:33:26,484 --> 00:33:29,403
You should've picked better friends,
you dumbass!

463
00:33:31,614 --> 00:33:33,074
Could be the car you smashed.

464
00:33:33,157 --> 00:33:35,785
Why would they go after his daughter
over that? You idiot!

465
00:33:38,746 --> 00:33:40,248
For fuck's sake.

466
00:33:41,749 --> 00:33:43,709
We need to reach him before the police do.

467
00:33:45,211 --> 00:33:47,713
Otherwise, fuck,
the money goes to the government.

468
00:33:52,593 --> 00:33:54,470
Don't worry. It'll be fine.

469
00:33:55,179 --> 00:33:56,848
Once everything's done,

470
00:33:57,348 --> 00:33:59,058
why don't we take a trip?

471
00:33:59,851 --> 00:34:01,853
You said you wanted to take a break.

472
00:34:02,353 --> 00:34:04,730
And we should let Da-eun see the world

473
00:34:05,231 --> 00:34:07,525
before she starts school.

474
00:34:13,990 --> 00:34:14,991
The police?

475
00:34:20,204 --> 00:34:22,540
I told you we just have to be patient
a bit longer.

476
00:34:22,623 --> 00:34:25,751
We were almost there.
Why couldn't you wait a few more days?!

477
00:34:25,835 --> 00:34:27,003
Why? Damn it!

478
00:34:38,514 --> 00:34:39,557
Shit.

479
00:34:53,362 --> 00:34:54,572
All day,

480
00:34:55,823 --> 00:34:59,619
all we had was a burger.

481
00:35:01,370 --> 00:35:02,663
I'm kinda hungry.

482
00:35:08,961 --> 00:35:10,630
Come on. Let's eat something.

483
00:35:14,383 --> 00:35:15,218
Are you buying?

484
00:35:15,968 --> 00:35:18,930
I've got no money.
Soo-hyun even blocked mobile payments.

485
00:35:19,013 --> 00:35:20,890
How did he get his hands on your phone?

486
00:35:21,682 --> 00:35:23,267
He bought me this phone.

487
00:35:23,351 --> 00:35:25,186
That was a stupid question.

488
00:35:30,858 --> 00:35:31,692
Give it to me.

489
00:35:32,235 --> 00:35:33,486
Give it!

490
00:35:34,695 --> 00:35:36,697
Huh? Hey! Why?

491
00:35:37,949 --> 00:35:39,575
No wonder his timing was perfect.

492
00:35:39,659 --> 00:35:42,203
He planted something on your phone,
you dumbass!

493
00:35:42,703 --> 00:35:44,080
He knew we were onto him!

494
00:35:44,163 --> 00:35:46,415
God, you stupid dumbass.

495
00:35:46,499 --> 00:35:48,042
Seriously! Goddamn it!

496
00:35:51,003 --> 00:35:52,672
Damn it.

497
00:35:55,508 --> 00:35:56,759
Still, you should've--

498
00:35:59,011 --> 00:36:00,263
What is it?

499
00:36:01,597 --> 00:36:03,307
Hey, go pick it up.

500
00:36:08,938 --> 00:36:10,022
It's over there.

501
00:36:20,574 --> 00:36:21,909
That fucking scared me.

502
00:36:21,993 --> 00:36:24,954
Why the hell does he keep calling me?
It's so annoying.

503
00:36:25,037 --> 00:36:25,955
Yes, sir.

504
00:36:26,038 --> 00:36:26,872
Where are you?

505
00:36:26,956 --> 00:36:29,166
You told me to follow up on the tip.

506
00:36:29,667 --> 00:36:31,210
You said it was a prank.

507
00:36:31,961 --> 00:36:33,212
Yes, I did.

508
00:36:33,296 --> 00:36:35,464
But something's bothering me.

509
00:36:35,548 --> 00:36:36,382
You slacking off?

510
00:36:37,550 --> 00:36:39,677
What the fuck do you mean? Seriously.

511
00:36:41,762 --> 00:36:43,180
Don't we have work to do?

512
00:36:43,264 --> 00:36:46,434
Everyone's working their asses off,
and you haven't shown up all day!

513
00:36:46,517 --> 00:36:47,852
-I mean--
-Hey.

514
00:36:47,935 --> 00:36:49,854
Just file the report as is and wrap it up.

515
00:36:49,937 --> 00:36:52,815
But I should at least meet that thug.

516
00:36:52,898 --> 00:36:55,609
How the fuck am I supposed
to write this report or whatever?

517
00:36:55,693 --> 00:36:57,778
Then did you at least find the bastard?

518
00:36:58,404 --> 00:36:59,989
ESCORT LADY
HE JUST CAME IN

519
00:37:01,699 --> 00:37:03,617
I found him. Yes. I just fucking did!

520
00:37:03,701 --> 00:37:04,535
I just found him!

521
00:37:04,618 --> 00:37:07,496
I'll file the report and close it out.
This is fucking bullshit.

522
00:37:09,081 --> 00:37:09,915
Huh?

523
00:37:21,177 --> 00:37:22,595
Just eat it already.

524
00:37:30,102 --> 00:37:31,228
Elders first.

525
00:37:31,312 --> 00:37:32,313
You bastard.

526
00:37:40,696 --> 00:37:41,864
Hey, hurry up and eat.

527
00:37:41,947 --> 00:37:43,074
We have to head out.

528
00:37:44,492 --> 00:37:45,493
We're going out again?

529
00:37:45,576 --> 00:37:47,328
-Where to?
-Somewhere.

530
00:37:49,080 --> 00:37:51,540
From now on,
don't ever tell me where we're going.

531
00:37:51,624 --> 00:37:53,084
Never ever tell me.

532
00:37:53,167 --> 00:37:54,627
If you do, I'll just--

533
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:55,711
Fishing.

534
00:37:58,881 --> 00:37:59,882
Eat up.

535
00:38:02,510 --> 00:38:03,469
I'm done.

536
00:38:13,187 --> 00:38:15,106
Did you get rid of the one at the morgue?

537
00:38:16,649 --> 00:38:17,483
No, not yet.

538
00:38:19,902 --> 00:38:21,320
Hurry up and burn it.

539
00:38:23,030 --> 00:38:23,864
Yes, sir.

540
00:38:35,084 --> 00:38:36,043
PRIVATE DETECTIVE AGENCY

541
00:38:36,585 --> 00:38:37,962
She said he was here. Damn it.

542
00:38:38,045 --> 00:38:40,172
The light's off. That lady…

543
00:38:58,023 --> 00:38:59,608
Who the hell is that?

544
00:39:00,484 --> 00:39:03,112
It's that bastard from yesterday.

545
00:39:03,195 --> 00:39:04,947
The one Noja beat the crap out of.

546
00:39:06,532 --> 00:39:08,284
So many new faces.

547
00:39:08,784 --> 00:39:10,244
That means things are fucked.

548
00:39:13,998 --> 00:39:15,499
Don't know him, huh?

549
00:39:15,583 --> 00:39:17,626
They were tearing into each other,

550
00:39:17,710 --> 00:39:19,211
and now they're friends?

551
00:39:19,295 --> 00:39:22,631
These bastards are just unbelievable.

552
00:39:48,032 --> 00:39:49,700
But how do you know he'll come?

553
00:39:49,783 --> 00:39:53,662
That bastard's very interested in you.
What you're doing and where you're going.

554
00:39:54,705 --> 00:39:57,875
He's tracking you all day on his phone.

555
00:39:59,752 --> 00:40:01,212
He's going to come check.

556
00:40:01,295 --> 00:40:02,379
Your dead body.

557
00:40:13,182 --> 00:40:16,477
GWANGNAM RESERVOIR

558
00:40:33,744 --> 00:40:34,995
Give me a tissue.

559
00:40:37,790 --> 00:40:39,583
Don't get too close, man.

560
00:40:39,667 --> 00:40:40,501
Yes, sir.

561
00:41:01,438 --> 00:41:02,731
This might take a while,

562
00:41:03,524 --> 00:41:05,317
so lie down and get comfortable.

563
00:41:11,156 --> 00:41:12,992
It's a good place to bury a body.

564
00:41:13,492 --> 00:41:16,078
You're dangerous, huh?
Must've buried a lot of bodies.

565
00:41:23,419 --> 00:41:24,837
Would they even care?

566
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:27,464
Wouldn't it be better for them if I died?

567
00:41:27,548 --> 00:41:30,384
If their goal was to kill you,
you'd be dead already.

568
00:41:31,468 --> 00:41:33,012
Since you can't die yet,

569
00:41:33,095 --> 00:41:35,055
they'll come here to check on you.

570
00:41:35,139 --> 00:41:36,974
That's the point of this fishing trip.

571
00:42:31,570 --> 00:42:34,239
Hey, Soo-hyun. It's me, Moon-jae.

572
00:42:34,323 --> 00:42:35,699
Can you talk for a moment?

573
00:42:36,200 --> 00:42:38,327
I need you to check something for me.

574
00:42:38,827 --> 00:42:40,496
Just in case.

575
00:43:24,039 --> 00:43:24,957
Got a bite.

576
00:49:02,711 --> 00:49:05,630
Subtitle translation by: Sung In Jang

